hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19187","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam. Sufyan once said: From Busr, or Busr ibn Mihjan. Then he used to say after: From Abu Mihjan al-Dili, from his father, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque, and prayer came. So he prayed, then said to me: Why did you not pray? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I had prayed at the lodging, then I came to you. He said: When you do so, pray with them and make it voluntary. My father said: Neither Abu Nuaym nor Abd al-Rahman said: And make it voluntary."
